That last call is the only `option<>` in this function without the create-if-missing `true`; lines 1039, 1044 and 1049 all pass it. Without it `option()` returns `nullptr` and `->values` dereferences null — which matches `RAX = 0` and `"filament"` sitting in `RCX`.

This file has no `different_settings_to_system` at all, so `size == 0` and the branch is always taken.

There is precedent for the fix. #14580 guarded four null dereferences of exactly this kind on the CLI path, including this very option, with the note:

> Read defensively — a 3mf missing preset ids (e.g. one produced by a non-GUI writer) would otherwise crash here on the deref.

    - current_filaments_name = config.option<ConfigOptionStrings>("filament_settings_id")->values;
    + if (const auto *o = config.option<ConfigOptionStrings>("filament_settings_id")) current_filaments_name = o->values;
The size itself costs nothing either way: the loop below only ever writes `different_settings[0]`, and `PresetBundle` re-resizes to `num_filaments + 2` from `filament_colour` regardless.

That turns the crash into "loads whatever parsed".

This is not a recent regression, so a bisect is not worth anyone's time. The line arrived already missing the `true`, in commit `a2431d796` (2023-02-14, lane.wei, "ENH: add logic to convert hybrid(auto) to tree(auto) for old 3mf"), and reached this repository through the merge `5ef51f6c8` (2023-03-07). The two lines were added together in that same hunk:

    +    ... this->option<ConfigOptionStrings>("different_settings_to_system", true)->values;
    +    size = this->option<ConfigOptionStrings>("filament_settings_id")->values.size() + 2;

I checked every commit that has touched `src/libslic3r/Config.cpp` — 46 at the time of writing — and only those two contain this line, so it has been unchanged for about three and a half years.

BambuStudio carries the same line. `bambulab/BambuStudio@master` has it verbatim at `Config.cpp:1096`, also without `true`, along with the same `break`. A PR is open there: bambulab/BambuStudio#12058 — the maintainer's preference there was a null check as well, which is what the diff above uses.

It survived this long because reaching it needs three things at once: a malformed array whose key sorts before `filament_settings_id` (here `extruder`, key 86 versus key 128), no `different_settings_to_system` in the file, and `is_project_settings`. Projects written by OrcaSlicer and BambuStudio emit well-formed arrays, so the path is only reached with a file from some other slicer.

Separately, worth your judgement: the `break` at line 1026 means one malformed key discards every key after it — here, 392 of them. A `continue` would keep the rest of a partially-bad config, but that is a real behaviour change and felt like your call rather than something to fold into a null-guard.

